d so for example one time I traded  my motorcycle sport bike nice great fun  motorcycle for 600 pounds of Lego but  before I did it I told her I said hey  I'm gonna  trade my motorcycle for all this Lego  and I'm just going to sell the Lego like  I'm not going to keep it I'm gonna sell  it and I'm gonna make a lot of profit  dude and you know I explained it to her  and her reaction was just like you know  okay  sounds like you've thought it through  you know and that's just been the story  the whole time and and that's why she's  my wife so so so yeah I mean it it helps  to have some sort of support when you're  trying to start your own and run your  own businesses or really do anything  that most people would perceive as risky  because most people are going to doubt  you I mean you're going to have you know  friends that support you and stuff but  for the most part most people will think  what you're doing is stupid crazy or  just isn't going to work or isn't a real  job all right so so having some sort of  support really does help and I think  that's probably all I'm going to really  say on that but I will say now getting  kind of into finance you know starting a  business is not something that you're  going to make a lot of money at  especially like you know someone asked  me how much money I make I'm really not  going to disclose that that would take a  really long time I have at least ten  income streams if not more so first of  all there's that also my income is  relatively volatile I mean over the  course of a year you can I can kind of  predict it out but it's pretty volatile  but I can say at least it goes up over  time my income at the moment goes up  about six to seven percent compounded  every single month that's insane  so when some people ask me like why I  don't take a job at like some Silicon  Valley company if you were to if you  first of all they can't give you that  much excitement right where all of my  energy all of my work goes into my own  equity I own 100% equity in my own  companies so all the energy and all the  work that I put into my companies I get  rewarded not immediately but almost  immediately like really quickly and it  and it only keeps building  top of that overtime like it just keeps  building up if you go to work for an  established company on like Facebook or  Apple or something you know they might  give you equity right they almost  certainly will but it's going to be a  tiny amount of equity and those  companies are you know they're not super  mature but they're not growing that much  compared to what they used to do right  when it was truly exciting and so they  came out for me that also if you were to  take my living income like I guess like  basically my income minus my expenses  right now I'm making pretty much the  same I would make if I went to go work  for like Google Apple Facebook you know  they're gonna pay you about six figures  probably like 120 to 150 starting on or  50,000 that is a year mmm  but then you have to factor in the cost  of living in a place like San Francisco  which is just absurd where rent is you  know three to five thousand dollars a  month it's just insane that's just rent  okay so so yeah so it you got to kind of  like think of those things but initially  starting out another reason why I'm not  going to break down exactly what I make  right now because what I make right now  is the the fruits of my labor from years  ago so if you were to take basically all  of the time I've put just into any one  of my businesses but let's just take the  YouTube channel in Python program in  that net if you took how much money I've  currently made today and divided it by  the number of hours that I've put into  it  you'd probably you'd find it's less than  minimum wage it's just less but if you  take maybe the amount of hours I've put  in in the last six months and the amount  of money I've made it's above minimum  wage now like I have worked and I've got  myself to the 